WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:06.094
"We face four historic crises all at the same time. This is going to take bold creative federal action."

00:00:06.094 --> 00:00:13.087
Use your full authority. The people of this nation&nbsp;have spoken. Now the work of making that vision is real.

00:00:13.087 --> 00:00:17.120
Now that the disastrous presidency&nbsp;of Donald Trump is likely coming to an end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:22.902
Joe Biden will get the chance to make good on&nbsp;his promise to create bold change in the lives&nbsp;of all Americans.

00:00:22.902 --> 00:00:28.169
On his first day in office, Biden says that he plans to roll back many of&nbsp;Trump's signature policies 

00:00:28.169 --> 00:00:32.443
with his own sweeping&nbsp;executive orders, and he has promised to transform&nbsp;the economy

00:00:32.443 --> 00:00:36.960
to fight climate change, reassert&nbsp;America's diplomatic and military power abroad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.221
and establish new federal offices like that of&nbsp;a national supply chain commander

00:00:41.221 --> 00:00:46.143
 to centralize control of commercial industry in response to&nbsp;the Coronavirus pandemic. 

00:00:46.143 --> 00:00:47.391
What is our mandate? 

00:00:47.391 --> 00:00:50.935
We're going to make historic investments so we'll seize the opportunity. 

00:00:50.935 --> 00:00:54.339
This will go down as one of the most progressive administrations in American history.

00:00:54.339 --> 00:00:57.997
It's unclear what Biden will ultimately&nbsp;be able to accomplish as president,

00:00:57.997 --> 00:01:02.000
but he has&nbsp;already spent 44 years as a senator and then&nbsp;vice president,

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.807
trying to bring transformative&nbsp;change through federal action in response to&nbsp;supposed crises,

00:01:06.807 --> 00:01:10.880
and his record on issues including&nbsp;immigration, the drug war, criminal justice reform,&nbsp;and foreign intervention

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:16.960
has been dismal. How can&nbsp;he really be a progressive and want to lock these&nbsp;people up?

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:24.461
And I'd say lock the S.O.B.'s up. Now we&nbsp; can find some fringe folks, libertarians, and&nbsp;left wingers in my party who say

00:01:24.461 --> 00:01:28.944
"No that's not&nbsp;we should do," but politically that consensus has&nbsp;been arrived at.

00:01:28.944 --> 00:01:33.144
As the president-elect pushes a&nbsp;new ambitious agenda it's worth remembering the&nbsp;impact

00:01:33.144 --> 00:01:37.680
of the far-reaching laws he has repeatedly&nbsp;helped pass which have created enormous suffering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:42.320
and exacerbated some of the most critical&nbsp;problems still afflicting American society.

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:47.334
We have predators on our streets. Increase&nbsp;the penalties, increase them.

00:01:47.334 --> 00:01:50.538
I would put the son of a gun in jail. Put them to death.

00:01:50.538 --> 00:01:55.936
We have to hold every drug user accountable because if there were no no drug users,

00:01:55.936 --> 00:01:59.273
there would&nbsp;be no appetite for drugs there would be no market for&nbsp;them.

00:01:59.273 --> 00:02:06.000
In the 80's Biden sought to escalate the&nbsp;drug war beyond what Ronald Reagan and George&nbsp;H.W. Bush&nbsp;had called for.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.920
The President says he&nbsp;wants to wage a war on drugs but if that's true,&nbsp;

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:13.529
what we need is another d-day not another vietnam.

00:02:13.529 --> 00:02:18.360
And co-sponsored legislation that locked up tens of thousands of predominantly young black men

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:19.681
for&nbsp;minor crack possession.

00:02:19.681 --> 00:02:25.253
Five years, no probation, no parole. If you have this much lock them up and put them in our prison.

00:02:25.253 --> 00:02:29.373
In the 90's he led the charge&nbsp;on a massive expansion of the death penalty.

00:02:29.373 --> 00:02:36.000
A wag in the newspaper recently wrote, "Biden&nbsp;has made it a death penalty offense for everything but jaywalking."

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.255
And the militarization of law enforcement.

00:02:38.255 --> 00:02:45.130
Let the FBI agents buy weapons as&nbsp;powerful as the drug cartels had.

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:46.410
They get beat up.

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:50.650
I wrote the original bill that started&nbsp;this whole process. The so-called Biden crime bill.

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:55.596
The 1994 crime bill along with several other&nbsp;pieces of legislation Biden pushed for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.596 --> 00:02:59.459
expanded mandatory minimum sentences, created three strikes&nbsp;laws,

00:02:59.459 --> 00:03:02.841
and drove up the local state and federal prison populations.

00:03:02.841 --> 00:03:06.451
Biden crime bill. The Biden&nbsp;crime bill. The Biden crime bill.

00:03:06.451 --> 00:03:15.179
Every major crime bill since 1976, every minor crime bill has had the&nbsp;name of the democratic senator

00:03:15.179 --> 00:03:17.192
 from the state of Delaware, Joe Biden. 

00:03:17.192 --> 00:03:21.370
In the 2000's Biden played a key role in expanding warrant-less surveillance.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:28.240
Just to set the record straight almost the same thing that&nbsp;got passed, the Patriot Act, was introduced by me

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:33.677
 in 1994. Including the wiretap changes and the rest.

00:03:33.677 --> 00:03:35.726
Starting disastrous foreign wars.

00:03:35.726 --> 00:03:40.960
Saddam Hussein is still seeking the accumulation of weapons of mass destruction.

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:45.560
I do not believe this is&nbsp;a rush to war I believe it's a march to peace and security.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:47.440
And building fences on the Mexican border.

00:03:52.626 --> 00:03:58.105
Biden's only solution to critical issues over&nbsp;nearly five decades has been to grow the federal&nbsp;government

00:03:58.105 --> 00:04:00.723
in an attempt to remake society for&nbsp;the better.

00:04:00.723 --> 00:04:05.486
In reality his agenda has destroyed vulnerable communities and eroded civil liberties.

00:04:05.486 --> 00:04:10.791
To hold our media accountable is something we all&nbsp;desire but there's a thing called the First Amendment,

00:04:10.791 --> 00:04:13.641
which is read in a way that I think&nbsp;is a little excessive.

00:04:13.641 --> 00:04:18.065
Though today his policy&nbsp;priorities have again shifted with the democratic&nbsp;political winds,

00:04:18.065 --> 00:04:21.440
what has held constant is&nbsp;Biden's commitment to bold state intervention&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:23.815
in more areas of Americans lives.

00:04:23.815 --> 00:04:30.000
These are interlocking crises of our time requires the president to defend us from every attack seen and unseen, 

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.396
always and without exception.

00:04:32.396 --> 00:04:35.723
And he's  never stopped telling us that it's all for our own&nbsp;good.

00:04:35.723 --> 00:04:40.405
The African-American community stood up again for me.

00:04:40.405 --> 00:04:44.529
You've always had my back and I have yours.

00:04:44.529 --> 00:04:54.365
They are in jail, away from my mother, your husband, our&nbsp;families. And my daughter will be safer,&nbsp;

00:04:54.365 --> 00:05:01.744
my wife will be safer, my mother will be&nbsp;
safer, and I will be safer, and I will be happy."

00:05:01.744 --> 00:05:06.847
Hand up, don't shoot. No justice, no peace.

00:05:06.847 --> 00:05:11.590
Watch out, watch out, watch out. 

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:25.327
The younger generation now tells me how&nbsp;tough things are, give me a break. No no.

00:05:25.327 --> 00:05:30.302
I have no empathy for it, give me a break because&nbsp;here's the deal guys,&nbsp;

00:05:30.302 --> 00:05:33.942
we decided we were going to change the world and we did.

00:05:33.942 --> 00:05:40.667
We did. We finished the civil rights movement to the first stage, the women's movement came to be.

00:05:40.667 --> 00:05:45.688
So my message&nbsp;is get involved. There's no place to hide.

